-# Geomantic Nodes (v0.3.82)
+# Geomantic Nodes (v0.3.83)
 - Use the approved second Blockbench model (`geomantic_node_model_v2`): one irregular stone lump with protruding amethyst crystals, approximately one block wide.
 - A node appears during generation of each vanilla amethyst geode. It is installed inside the geode's air cavity near the origin.
 - A Node is a block entity with custom-mesh rendering, slow rotation, and gentle hovering motion.
 - Wand right-click grants **+5 permanent maximum Mana** and **+1 Arcane Knowledge** to the player.
-- Attunement works once per player per Node; other players can use the same Node once.
-- Rewards require an Awakened player. Claimed player UUIDs persist in the Node block entity across saves.
-- The maximum Mana bonus also survives player death.
+- A successful attunement consumes and removes the Node immediately. The Node cannot be used by another player.
+- Rewards require an Awakened player. Unawakened players cannot consume the Node.
+- Existing per-player claim NBT remains backward-compatible but is no longer used because attunement removes the Node.
+- The permanent maximum Mana bonus also survives player death.
+- Node consumption does not drop a block item; it vanishes on use.
 - These nodes are independent of High Mana Zones.
 - Gnome village generation is not implemented yet. Future village generation will create its own Node rather than require a natural geode.
